$DIR/main.p:25:7: cannot move package variable global: only a local variable can be moved out of
    Buf is an owner type, so using global here would move it. But a package
    variable lives for the whole program and would still believe it holds the
    value.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    To move it out and leave an empty value in its place:
        v := take(&global)
    To look at it without moving it:
        v := &global
    To copy it:
        v := global.Clone()
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3303" for a longer explanation)
